/-!
# The deeper face field of the multiple sine is translation stable

The descending face induction runs its difference system on the differential field generated by the
packets of an upward-closed family of faces.  Every structural translation must map that field into
itself.  Two cases: a direction of the face permutes its packet, and a surviving direction moves a
packet element by its displacement into the next packet, up to the rational coordinate field.  An
upward-closed family therefore has a translation-stable field.
-/

open Filter Set Topology Complex
open scoped Differential

namespace GaloisForLFunctions.HTGeometry

open GaloisForLFunctions Bottcher
